-- Scene 4: the title is bigger than its subtitle, and SetFont is why --
   stzCanvas's SetFont behaves exactly like Fill: with a shape PENDING it
   restyles that shape; with none pending it sets the canvas default. So
   a run of labels that styles BEFORE adding is off by one -- every call
   resizes the label before it, and the plate's title came out smaller
   than its own subtitle.

   ONE TEXT RUN IS ONE PATH in the output, so a label's height is the
   vertical span of its path -- which is the thing that was wrong.
   'Hxy' added then styled at 28 px is 26.2000 px tall; at 11 px, 10.2900
  [ok]   asking for a bigger font gets a bigger glyph
   on an empty canvas the wrong order still gives 26.2000 px
  [ok]   which is why the bug survived a casual look
   but in a RUN, asking for 28 then 11 draws 10.2900 px then 26.2000
  [ok]   the first label does NOT get the size it asked for
  [ok]   and the second wears the first one's size
   on a real plate: the title's H is 11.9000 px, the subtitle's 8.4000
  [ok]   so the plate adds first and styles second

